Markdown tables cannot hold code blocks; targets put them there.

| JavaScript | Python |
|---|---|
| @target[js] | @target[py] |

The same source three times, in a table with no header row:

| @target[js] | @target[js] | 🎯short |

And in running text, a one-line source stays inline: @target[short].

@begin(source){target=js}
```js
let x = 1;
```
@end(source)

@begin(source){target=py}
First a paragraph.

```python
x = 1
```
@end(source)

@begin(source){target=short}
just *words*
@end(source)
